 # Verification Report
 
-The local gallery was checked for current title and navigation labels, current button hierarchy, RTL, reduced motion, 320/200% inspection, JSON validity, local dependencies, and no horizontal overflow in the inspected browser state. The package is a visual foundation and does not claim physical Samsung-device or screen-reader verification.
+Regenerated by execution run `run-20260913-msv2-zai-01` (Waves 0–C) on branch `micro-standard-v2-execution-20260913`, from the tests actually executed.
+
+## Environment
+
+Headless Chromium (Playwright), viewports 320/360/390/430px at 844px height; text scales 100/130/200%; RTL and LTR; reduced-motion control and `prefers-reduced-motion` emulation. This is local browser evidence only.
+
+## What was verified
+
+1. **Token integrity** — every custom property consumed by the gallery resolves against `design-tokens.css` (0 unresolved; 62 were undefined before this run). Hex audit: the approved set is 18 values, byte-identical to baseline; zero new hex introduced. `design-tokens.json`, `MANIFEST.json`, `coverage-matrix.json` parse as valid JSON.
+2. **Contrast** — 19 token pairs computed (WCAG 2.1 relative luminance); the 13 documented claims match the computed values to the digit (warm ink/canvas 17.50, warm ink/surface 18.43, Clay/surface 3.12 non-text-only, Clay interactive/surface 3.90 edge-only, error/surface 6.02, info 3.87, status 3.25, success 3.27 non-text-only, boundary 3.65; ordinary-save pair 16.72; commit pair 18.43).
+3. **Action classes** — computed styles in the running gallery: Create Clay `rgb(217,119,87)` with pressed `rgb(201,100,66)`; Save surface `rgb(245,244,237)` with ink `rgb(20,20,19)` and pressed inset 2px `rgb(201,100,66)` edge; commit fill `rgb(20,20,19)`; selected chip/segment/nav use the Clay edge, never black fills.
+4. **Interactions** — loading keeps the Warm Tint surface with `aria-busy` and blocks duplicate submits; quiet completion shows check + past-tense word and restores the original label; chart cycles data → zero (+ text alternative) → no data → loading; sheet, dialog (Escape/focus), snackbar, segmented, rail, and nav switching all function; zero console/page errors.
+5. **Geometry** — no horizontal overflow at 320/360/390/430px, including 200% text scale at 320px; FAB is 56px Clay in its own gutter.
+6. **Reduced motion** — transitions/animations collapse to 0.00001s under the control and the system preference; labels, markers, and `aria-busy` preserve meaning.
+7. **Scrim** — previously invisible (undefined token); now renders `rgba(20,20,19,0.45)`.
+
+## What was not tested (explicitly not claimed)
+
+- Physical Samsung-device testing — not performed.
+- Screen-reader (assistive technology) testing — not performed; `aria-*` usage was checked in markup only.
+- Real-device performance, font rendering on Arabic device fonts, and PWA behavior — outside this package.
+
+The package is a visual foundation and does not claim financial policy correctness; product semantics remain Micro-owned.
